\section{Perturbation Analysis}
Stochastic perturbations in $S$ propagate along characteristic velocity vectors without global instability. Variations in $\gamma_{extinct}$ introduce local exponential damping without inducing stiffness. CFL-adaptive time-stepping ensures TVD behavior under sharp gradients.

\section{Stress Testing}
Synthetic stress tests increased ingestion load to $10.2\times10^9$ sources, gravitational computation to $1.2\times10^9$ nodes, and habitability evaluation to $8.5\times10^8$ tracks. PDE saturation maintained $60\,$FPS under maximal wavefront overlap.

\section{Results}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Ingestion throughput: $450\times10^6$ sources/sec.
    \item Octree latency: $1.4\,$ms.
    \item GPU utilization: $99.2\%$.
    \item PDE stability: zero divergence.
    \item Total simulated time: $13.8\,$Gyr.
\end{itemize}

\section{Reproducibility}
Deterministic floating-point execution (IEEE 754-2008), fixed PRNG seeding, and hardware-independent compute shaders guarantee bit-level reproducibility across compliant GPU architectures.

